# GetRandomTrip — Project Rules

Full reference: `AGENTS.md` at repo root.

## Stack
Next.js 16 App Router · TypeScript strict · Prisma 7 + PostgreSQL · NextAuth 4 ·
Zustand 5 (slices) · Shadcn UI + Radix + Tailwind · Vitest + happy-dom · Netlify

## Naming
- Folders: `kebab-case`
- Components: `PascalCase.tsx`
- Helpers / utils: `camelCase.ts`
- Hooks: `useCamelCase.ts`
- Constants: `SNAKE_CASE.ts`
- Types: `PascalCase.ts`

## Component rules
- One component per file. Files ≤ 300 lines.
- No barrel `index.ts` files — import by direct path.
- Page files are thin orchestrators (fetch + layout only, no inline UI logic).
- File order: imports → types/interfaces → routing vars → Zustand → useState →
  derived → memoized → hooks → useEffect → handleX → refs → JSX return.

## `"use client"` — only when strictly necessary
Use for: interactivity, Web APIs, Zustand reads, local useState/useEffect.
Never use for: data fetching, static display, layout, utility functions.

## JSX props — alphabetical order (always)
```tsx
<Button aria-label="x" disabled={x} onClick={fn} size="lg" />
```

## Tailwind classes
- Alphabetical within each group.
- Responsive/state prefixes in separate `cn()` strings:
```tsx
className={cn('flex gap-4 rounded-xl', 'md:flex-row', 'hover:bg-gray-50')}
```

## TypeScript
- Strict mode. Run `npm run typecheck` before committing.
- Manual types in `src/lib/types/`. Never import `@prisma/client` in UI code.
- Prefer `interface` over `type`. Avoid enums — use const maps.

## Zustand
- Slice per file in `src/store/slices/`. Each slice has a typed interface.
- Composed in `src/store/store.ts` with `devtools` + `persist`.
- Action naming: `setX`, `clearX`, `updateX`.

## Auth (server-side)
```ts
const session = await getServerSession(authOptions);
if (!session) redirect('/login');
if (!hasRoleAccess(session.user.role, ['ADMIN'])) return forbidden();
```

## i18n
- All user-visible strings must use dictionary keys — no hardcoded text.
- Add keys to both `src/dictionaries/en.json` and `src/dictionaries/es.json`.

## Images
- Never use raw `<img>`. Always use `<Img>` from `@/components/common/Img`.
- Remote hostnames must be added to `next.config.js` `remotePatterns`.

## Design system constraints
- No dark mode. Never add `dark:` Tailwind variants.
- Color tokens: gray-900 (ink), text-light-blue (cyan), yellow-400 (sun), white
  (surface), gray-50 (ground), gray-200 (border).
- `GlassCard` is marketing-only — never in dashboard pages.
- Status badges always render through `<StatusIndicatorBadge>`.
- Icons from `lucide-react`.

## Quality gate (every PR)
- `npm run typecheck` → zero errors
- `npm run lint` → zero errors
- `npm run test` → all pass
- Both `en.json` and `es.json` updated for any new copy
- Responsive ≥ 360 px mobile, ≥ 1280 px desktop
- Empty and error states handled

## Commits
Conventional format: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`
No AI attribution in commit messages or PR descriptions.
